# Frontend (Vite — active) + legacy Next.js webui (rollback only)

The cutover is **complete as of phase 7** — see
[frontend/CUTOVER.md](mdc:frontend/CUTOVER.md). The Vite app is now
the only operator UI; the legacy Next.js webui is stopped and kept
in `docker-compose.yml` for one-command rollback only.

| App | Local dev | Compose host port | State | Source of truth |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| [frontend/](mdc:frontend) | `pnpm --dir frontend dev` (`:3001`) | `:3002` | active | [frontend/CUTOVER.md](mdc:frontend/CUTOVER.md), [docs/webui.md](mdc:docs/webui.md) |
| [webui/](mdc:webui) | `pnpm --dir webui dev` (`:3000`) | `:3000` (stopped) | rollback only | — |

All new routes go to `frontend/`. Do not add new pages to `webui/` —
its only purpose now is rollback. If you need a feature `frontend/`
doesn't have yet, add it to `frontend/`.

## Hard rules

1. **WebSocket pipeline is throttled.** Use the existing
   rAF-batched, 30 FPS-capped consumer in
   [frontend/src/lib/ws/](mdc:frontend/src/lib/ws) (`useLiveStream`,
   `useChatStream`, `throttle`). The ring buffer is bounded —
   recency wins over completeness for tick / order-book streams.
   Don't add a raw `WebSocket` listener that pushes every frame to
   React state.
2. **Kill-switch fan-out is non-negotiable.** The topbar
   `KillSwitch` component
   ([frontend/src/components/common/KillSwitch.tsx](mdc:frontend/src/components/common/KillSwitch.tsx))
   is the canonical halt surface. The wired backend route today is
   `POST /portfolio/kill_switch` (in
   [aqp/api/routes/portfolio.py](mdc:aqp/api/routes/portfolio.py)).
   The design contract is per-runtime fan-out as new endpoints come
   online:
   - `/agents/halt`
   - `/paper/stop-all`
   - `/bots/halt-all`
   - `/rl/halt-all`
   When you wire a new endpoint from the design list, add it to
   `KillSwitch` in the same PR. New runtime-bearing services must
   be added to this list when they ship.
3. **Sandbox / Paper mode is globally indicated.** Whenever the
   active session is sandbox / paper:
   - Amber outline around the app shell
   - Tab-title prefix (e.g. `[PAPER]`)
   - "Simulated execution" caption on every order ticket
   The user must never confuse paper for live. This is a guardrail,
   not a cosmetic preference.
4. **Manual order tickets are gated by typed-confirmation
   friction.** No one-click `BUY 100 AAPL` button. The user types
   the symbol or the size to confirm.
5. **Numeric surfaces use semantic financial colour tokens +
   tabular-figure font features.** Greens / reds are from the
   defined token palette so colour-blind operators see consistent
   shapes; numbers always use `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums`
   so digits don't shift width.
6. **OHLC charts use `lightweight-charts`** (WebGL renderer),
   declared once in
   [frontend/](mdc:frontend) and re-used. Don't pull in a different
   charting lib without a parity migration plan.
7. **The browser-side IDE uses CodeMirror 6.** Don't introduce
   Monaco for new surfaces — bundle size + duplicate indent /
   keymap UX.

## API client + types

- Type-safe REST client comes from `openapi-typescript` +
  `openapi-fetch` in `frontend/`, regenerated from
  `python -m scripts.export_openapi` via `make webui-gen-api`.
- WebSocket hooks (`useChatStream`, `useLiveStream`) wrap
  `/chat/stream/{task_id}` and `/live/stream/{channel_id}` with
  reconnect + backoff. Use them; don't open raw sockets.
- After changing FastAPI routes, regenerate types **in the same
  PR** that touches the `frontend/` consumer. Stale types compile
  but ship runtime mismatches.

## CORS

CORS is env-driven via `AQP_WEBUI_CORS_ORIGINS`. Empty falls back to
`*` for back-compat — fine in dev, not in prod. Don't hardcode origins.

## Don't

- Don't ship a new chart lib next to `lightweight-charts`.
- Don't bypass the throttled WS pipeline for "this stream is
  small". Today's small stream is tomorrow's hot path.
- Don't remove the sandbox indicator to "clean up the UI".
- Don't add pages that talk to the Celery broker directly. Go
  through FastAPI per
  [tasks-api.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/tasks-api.mdc).
- Don't drop the kill-switch from the topbar in any new shell
  layout. It's a hard guardrail.
- Don't shadow the Action Center pattern with a parallel
  notifications surface. Add to the existing `/action-center`.
